  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Kansas has received $76.9M in federal contract obligations so far in FY2027 to date. The state recorded 2,237 awards with an average award size of $34.4K. Obligations fell 98.0% year over year compared with prior full fiscal years that ranged from $3.1B to $4.3B. Fiscal-year obligations were $4.3B in FY22, $3.1B in FY23, $3.4B in FY24, $3.7B in FY25, and $3.8B in FY26. The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $54.4M, followed by the Environmental Protection Agency with $11.9M and the Department of Labor with $2.4M. FEDERAL EXPRESS CORPORATION is the largest vendor with $19.9M, and A-TEAM SOLUTIONS LLC obligated $12.6M. Couriers and Express Delivery Services lead industries with $19.9M, Facilities Support Services account for $12.8M, and Remediation Services account for $10.8M. All figures are contract obligations; current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has federal contracting in Kansas changed since prior years?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 98.0% year over year in FY2027 to date. Kansas obligations were $4.3B in FY22, $3.1B in FY23, $3.4B in FY24, $3.7B in FY25, and $3.8B in FY26, compared with $76.9M in FY27 to date. Award volume remained measurable with 2,237 awards and an average award size of $34.4K. The current totals are partial because fiscal year to date figures are not final."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which buyers, vendors, and industries lead contracting in Kansas right now?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the top buyer with $54.4M, followed by the Environmental Protection Agency with $11.9M and the Department of Labor with $2.4M. FEDERAL EXPRESS CORPORATION is the top vendor with $19.9M, A-TEAM SOLUTIONS LLC follows with $12.6M, and FEDEX SUPPLY CHAIN DISTRIBUTION SYSTEM, INC. has $8.6M. Couriers and Express Delivery Services lead industries with $19.9M, Facilities Support Services have $12.8M, and Remediation Services have $10.8M."
